Subject: [PATCH 360/488] DeepSeek-V4.1: Score DSpark's drafts with the
 TileLang confidence head

The DS4.1 drafter builds its confidence head through
kernels.dspark_confidence_head(), so under the TileLang family every draft
step's acceptance probabilities come from one TileLang launch instead of
ATen's concatenation, FP32 copy and sigmoid around cuBLAS's dot product and
reduction (one stream) or GEMV (sixteen streams). The head's weight loads as
before; the module declares its kernel for preparation.

The sum is FP32 in a fixed order per draft, so a draft's probability, and the
draft budget and dead rows adaptive verification derives from rank 0's, no
longer depend on how many requests the step drafts for. It is not cuBLAS's
order: a probability may differ from the previous release's in its last bits
(within 2^-18 in the tests), which can change which drafts a step verifies but
not a temperature-0 token.
---
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/nvidia/dspark.py | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/nvidia/dspark.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/nvidia/dspark.py
index 01827bfb3..230cf4b60 100644
--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/nvidia/dspark.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/nvidia/dspark.py
@@ -431,8 +431,9 @@ class DSparkDeepseekV4Model(nn.Module):
         )
         self.confidence_head: DSparkConfidenceHead | None = None
         if getattr(config, "enable_confidence_head", True):
-            self.confidence_head = DSparkConfidenceHead(
-                config.hidden_size + config.dspark_markov_rank,
+            self.confidence_head = kernels.dspark_confidence_head(
+                config.hidden_size,
+                config.dspark_markov_rank,
                 prefix=maybe_prefix(prefix, "confidence_head"),
             )
 
